        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Treadmill cleaning goes wrong in two ways: a product that leaves a slippery film on the
          belt, and liquid that finds its way into the console or the motor compartment. Neither
          needs a special treadmill cleaner to avoid. Almost everything a home treadmill needs is a
          few drops of mild soap, a stack of microfibre cloths, a screen-safe cleaner and a small
          vacuum with a crevice tool, with gym wipes as an optional extra for shared machines. The
          five picks below cover those jobs, and the guide after them explains which product goes
          where, and which ones never belong on a treadmill at all.
        </p>

