        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Keep it mild, soft and dry.</strong> A mild dish soap, a pack of
            microfibre cloths and, for a touchscreen, an alcohol- and ammonia-free screen cleaner
            handle every surface you touch. A small vacuum with a crevice tool handles the dust that
            actually shortens a treadmill's life, and gym wipes earn their place only on a shared
            machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Never put silicone spray, WD-40, polish or solvents on the belt, never spray anything at
            the console, and unplug before anything more than a quick wipe. For the deck and the
            motor hood, follow the dedicated guides, starting with
            <a href="/how-to-clean-under-treadmill-belt/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">cleaning under the belt</a>.
          </p>
